From ec5c1b4940460197d0fe707fec61274e4093c790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:26:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the GnuPG-based %gpgverify with %openpgpverify, which uses
Sequoia sqv and takes the same options, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Release bumped with a changelog entry.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 grep.spec | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/grep.spec b/grep.spec
index d4344e5..3b7a3b0 100644
--- a/grep.spec
+++ b/grep.spec
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 Summary: Pattern matching utilities
 Name: grep
 Version: 3.12
-Release: 4%{?dist}
+Release: 5%{?dist}
 License: GPL-3.0-or-later AND LGPL-3.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later AND GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.0-or-later AND GFDL-1.3-no-invariants-or-later
 URL: https://www.gnu.org/software/grep/
 
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ Buildrequires: glibc-all-langpacks
 BuildRequires: perl(FileHandle)
 BuildRequires: make
 BuildRequires: gnupg2
+BuildRequires: openpgpverify
 # https://fedorahosted.org/fpc/ticket/174
 Provides: bundled(gnulib)
 # for backward compatibility (rhbz#1540485)
@@ -47,7 +48,7 @@ prints the matching lines. GNU's grep utilities include grep, egrep and fgrep.
 GNU grep is needed by many scripts, so it shall be installed on every system.
 
 %prep
-%{gpgverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
+%{openpgpverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
 %autosetup -p1
 
 %build
@@ -89,6 +90,9 @@ make check
 %{_libexecdir}/grepconf.sh
 
 %changelog
+* Mon Oct 12 2026 Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com> - 3.12-5
+- Verify upstream source signatures with openpgpverify
+
 * Thu Jul 16 2026 Fedora Release Engineering <releng@fedoraproject.org> - 3.12-4
 - Rebuilt for https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Fedora_45_Mass_Rebuild
 
-- 
2.56.0

